course: dictionary
lesson: 15804
title: Unbecoming: not suitable or not nice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unbecoming has two parts: un- means not, and becoming here means suitable or looking nice. So unbecoming means not suitable or not nice. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «It was unbecoming of the referee to shout rude words at the players.» The referee's job is to be fair and calm, so shouting rude words is not suitable for a referee.
explain: Context can also tell you about clothes. «Her bright orange hat was unbecoming with her red hair.» The orange and red clash, so the hat does not look nice on her. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the hard word. Does «not suitable» or «did not look nice» still make sense?
explain: This word is formal and a little old-fashioned, so you will mostly meet it in rules, stories and serious writing. In everyday talk, people say «not right» or «doesn't suit you» instead. Knowing both helps you understand the old word and say the same idea in your own words.
fact: Unbecoming starts with un-, which means not.
fact: «Unbecoming» means not suitable or proper for a person in a certain role, such as a teacher, officer or guest.
fact: «Unbecoming» can also mean that clothes or colours do not look nice on the person wearing them.
fact: The word is formal and old-fashioned, so it is often found in rules and older stories.
fact: Everyday words for «unbecoming» include «not right» and «doesn't suit you».
exercise: «It was unbecoming of the referee to shout rude words at the players.» What does unbecoming mean here? | *Not suitable for a referee | Loud, like a whistle | Funny and silly | Very kind and helpful
exercise: «Her bright orange hat was unbecoming with her red hair.» What does unbecoming suggest about the hat? | It was very old | *It did not look nice on her | It was made of wool | It made her look fine and tidy
exercise: «Her rude joke was unbecoming of a guest at the party.» Find and copy the word that means not suitable. | party | guest | joke | *unbecoming
test: What does unbecoming mean in «unbecoming of a teacher»? | Very clever and quick | Late for school | Kind and generous to everyone | *Not suitable or proper for a teacher
test: Sam says the yellow scarf is unbecoming. What does he mean? | *It does not suit him | It is too warm to wear | It is brand new | It has no pockets
exam: Which word best replaces unbecoming in «It was unbecoming of the officer to yell at his men»? | Hungry | Cheerful | Gentle | *Improper
